# Maths in TeX headings

PDF bookmarks cannot carry TeX maths. When writing or editing `.tex` files, wrap every equation or expression in a sectioning command with `\texorpdfstring`. Use an empty PDF argument.

```latex
\texorpdfstring{$equation or expression$}{}
```

Applies to `\section`, `\subsection`, `\subsubsection`, and any other heading that `hyperref` writes to the outline. Use the same wrap in `\caption` when the caption contains maths.

## Examples

BAD:

```latex
\subsection{$H_1$ Loop Detection}
\section{Canonical Form and the $\kappa \leftrightarrow 1/\kappa$ Symmetry}
```

GOOD:

```latex
\subsection{\texorpdfstring{$H_1$}{} Loop Detection}
\section{Canonical Form and the \texorpdfstring{$\kappa \leftrightarrow 1/\kappa$}{} Symmetry}
\label{sec:canonical}
```

Do not leave raw `$...$` in a heading. Do not put a prose fallback in the second argument unless a journal template requires a non-empty bookmark string.